WEBVTT

00:02.550 --> 00:03.551
KATARA: Water.

00:04.928 --> 00:05.929
Earth.

00:06.846 --> 00:07.847
Fire.

00:08.890 --> 00:09.891
Air.

00:11.434 --> 00:15.396
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

00:15.522 --> 00:18.566
Then, everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

00:19.859 --> 00:22.487
Only the Avatar,
master of all four elements,

00:22.612 --> 00:23.821
could stop them.

00:23.947 --> 00:26.241
But when the world
needed him most, he vanished.

00:27.575 --> 00:29.702
A hundred years passed,
and my brother and I discovered

00:29.827 --> 00:32.914
the new Avatar,
an Airbender named Aang.

00:33.039 --> 00:35.250
And although
his airbending skills are great,

00:35.375 --> 00:37.669
he has a lot to learn before
he's ready to save anyone.

00:37.794 --> 00:39.003
AANG: Oof!

00:39.128 --> 00:42.090
KATARA: But I believe
Aang can save the world.

00:42.215 --> 00:45.718
♪

00:48.141 --> 00:51.228
♪

01:06.076 --> 01:07.535
Top of the morning, Momo!

01:07.661 --> 01:09.037
Sounds like you slept well.

01:09.162 --> 01:10.497
Like a baby moose lion.

01:10.622 --> 01:12.624
I'm ready to face the Fire Lord.

01:12.749 --> 01:14.918
So what's your strategy
for taking him down?

01:15.043 --> 01:16.753
Going to get your glow on
and hit him with

01:16.878 --> 01:18.338
a little Avatar State action?

01:18.463 --> 01:19.547
I can't.

01:19.673 --> 01:21.299
When Azula shot me
with lightning,

01:21.424 --> 01:23.927
my seventh chakra was locked,
cutting off my connection

01:24.052 --> 01:26.263
to all the cosmic energy
in the Universe.

01:27.138 --> 01:28.556
You know what I just heard?

01:28.682 --> 01:32.018
Blah-blah spiritual mumbo jumbo,
blah-blah something about space.

01:33.270 --> 01:34.604
KATARA: Oh no.

01:34.688 --> 01:37.315
Sokka, do you think the fog
will delay the invasion?

01:38.566 --> 01:41.403
No, that is the invasion.

01:41.528 --> 01:46.992
♪

01:52.122 --> 01:53.707
KATARA: You made it, Dad!

01:53.832 --> 01:56.084
Were you able to locate
everyone I told you to find?

01:56.376 --> 01:59.129
I did, but I'm
a little worried, Sokka.

01:59.254 --> 02:01.881
Some of these men
aren't exactly the warrior type.

02:02.007 --> 02:04.092
Whooo-wheee.

02:04.217 --> 02:06.636
This place ain't nothing
like a swamp.

02:06.761 --> 02:08.263
What'd you reckon that is, Tho?

02:08.388 --> 02:09.889
Some sort of Fire Nation
exploding trap

02:10.015 --> 02:11.224
that would eat ya?

02:11.349 --> 02:13.143
It's just a rock, Due.

02:13.268 --> 02:15.520
Well, I'll be.

02:15.645 --> 02:17.439
Is it just me,
or are those fellas

02:17.564 --> 02:19.357
a little loose in the leaf hat?

02:19.482 --> 02:22.110
I just wish
they would wear pants.

02:22.235 --> 02:24.404
Pants are an illusion.

02:24.529 --> 02:26.364
And so is death.

02:28.658 --> 02:29.993
HARU: Hi, Katara.

02:32.037 --> 02:34.247
Haru, it's so good to see you.

02:34.372 --> 02:35.790
Toph, this is Haru.

02:35.915 --> 02:38.168
When we met him, his town was
controlled by the Fire Nation.

02:38.293 --> 02:39.878
So we had to hide
his Earth-bending.

02:40.003 --> 02:43.340
Katara inspired me and my
father to take back our village.

02:43.465 --> 02:46.259
You helped us find
our courage, Katara.

02:46.384 --> 02:48.928
Now we're here to help you.

02:50.305 --> 02:52.849
No way. Is that―

02:53.058 --> 02:55.935
Hippo happy
to see Blind Bandit!

02:56.061 --> 02:57.729
You guys here for a rematch?

02:57.854 --> 02:59.397
Negatory.

02:59.522 --> 03:02.650
The Boulder and The Hippo
no longer fight

03:02.776 --> 03:04.486
for others' entertainment.

03:04.611 --> 03:07.530
Now, we fight for our Kingdom!

03:08.031 --> 03:09.366
Sweet!

03:09.491 --> 03:11.326
♪

03:11.618 --> 03:13.370
[ crash ]

03:15.205 --> 03:18.875
[ coughing ]

03:23.380 --> 03:24.464
Was that a new invention?

03:24.589 --> 03:25.924
Yes.

03:26.049 --> 03:29.552
But unfortunately,
the incendiary capabilities

03:29.677 --> 03:32.514
of peanut sauce
proved to be a failure.

03:32.639 --> 03:34.599
You're making
peanut sauce bombs?

03:34.724 --> 03:35.892
They're destructive.

03:36.017 --> 03:37.560
And delicious!

03:37.685 --> 03:39.938
BOTH: [ slurps and laughs ]

03:40.146 --> 03:42.399
Were you able to complete work
on the plans I sent you?

03:42.732 --> 03:44.025
Yes, I was.

03:44.150 --> 03:47.278
And I think the Fire Nation
will be quite surprised.

03:47.404 --> 03:49.614
Aang, my dad and I
made this for you.

03:49.739 --> 03:53.576
♪

03:53.701 --> 03:54.744
A new glider!

03:54.869 --> 03:56.371
This is amazing.

03:56.496 --> 04:00.291
And as a special feature,
I added a snack compartment.

04:02.419 --> 04:04.879
Oh well, I'm sure
that will come in handy.

04:07.841 --> 04:10.844
I bet you're tired of
being in that cell, old man.

04:10.969 --> 04:12.804
Well, too bad.

04:12.929 --> 04:16.099
You're never stepping
outside these walls again.

04:16.224 --> 04:17.684
Breakfast.

04:18.935 --> 04:20.270
Don't get too close.

04:20.395 --> 04:22.480
His stench will
knock you right out.

04:22.605 --> 04:23.940
[ chuckles ]

04:25.442 --> 04:27.235
I snuck in some white jade tea.

04:27.360 --> 04:30.113
I know you like rare teas.

04:30.238 --> 04:31.865
IROH: Thank you, Ming.

04:31.990 --> 04:36.619
Ever since I was put in here,
you have been very kind to me.

04:36.744 --> 04:41.416
♪

04:42.000 --> 04:43.126
[ gulps nervously ]

04:43.251 --> 04:45.295
Don't worry, you'll do great.

04:45.420 --> 04:48.506
[ deep breath ]

04:48.631 --> 04:49.632
Good morning, everyone!

04:49.757 --> 04:50.884
Ah!

04:53.595 --> 04:55.013
Um...

04:55.138 --> 04:58.975
So, as you know, today
we're invading the Fire Nation.

04:59.100 --> 05:00.393
I mean I know you know that.

05:00.518 --> 05:01.895
Because otherwise why else
would you be here.

05:02.020 --> 05:03.688
[ laughs ] Anyway...

05:06.858 --> 05:08.359
The Fire Lord's palace is here.

05:08.485 --> 05:10.987
Uh no, uh wait―uh
wait―uh wait, it's here.

05:11.112 --> 05:12.864
And, uh, there's
an eclipse today.

05:12.989 --> 05:14.657
And Aang's going
to fight the Fire Lord.

05:14.782 --> 05:16.868
And the Firebenders
won't have any fire to use,

05:16.951 --> 05:18.244
so that's good for us.

05:18.328 --> 05:22.540
And um―I'm sorry, let me
start at the beginning.

05:23.500 --> 05:25.502
Katara and I discovered
Aang frozen in an iceberg.

05:25.627 --> 05:27.962
Now I didn't like Aang at first,
but I grew to love him over time,

05:28.087 --> 05:29.255
then we went over
to the Southern Air Temple,

05:29.339 --> 05:30.798
where Aang used to live,
and then we met Suki,

05:30.882 --> 05:33.426
-who is a Kyoshi warrior.
- Wow, when he says beginning,

05:33.510 --> 05:35.428
he means
the beginning beginning.

05:35.553 --> 05:37.722
SOKKA: ...got Haru arrested, and
then now he's grown a mustache.

05:37.847 --> 05:40.391
- And if you look in the front―
- HAKODA: Thank you, Sokka.

05:40.517 --> 05:43.394
It's okay, why don't
you take a break?

05:43.520 --> 05:46.189
Let me just clarify
a few points for everyone.

05:46.314 --> 05:49.150
Today is the Day of Black Sun.

05:49.275 --> 05:51.694
And I want to thank you all
for your self-sacrifice

05:51.819 --> 05:53.404
and your courage.

05:53.530 --> 05:55.365
There are two steps
to the invasion.

05:55.490 --> 05:58.701
A naval stage
and then a land stage.

05:58.826 --> 06:01.120
To gain sea access
to the Fire Nation capital,

06:01.246 --> 06:05.083
we have to get past
our first major obstacle here.

06:05.208 --> 06:07.210
The Great Gates of Azulon.

06:07.335 --> 06:10.046
Next, we hit the land,
and we hit hard.

06:10.171 --> 06:11.631
We must fight
past their battlements

06:11.756 --> 06:13.925
and secure the plaza tower.

06:14.050 --> 06:16.719
Once we do that,
it's up to the royal palace.

06:16.844 --> 06:19.013
At that point,
the eclipse will begin.

06:19.556 --> 06:20.974
Excuse me.

06:21.099 --> 06:23.476
The Boulder is confused.

06:23.601 --> 06:27.063
Isn't the point to invade
during the eclipse?

06:27.188 --> 06:29.899
When the Firebenders
are powerless?

06:30.024 --> 06:32.026
The eclipse
only lasts eight minutes.

06:32.151 --> 06:34.028
Not enough time
for the whole invasion.

06:34.153 --> 06:37.198
And the royal palace is heavily
guarded by Firebenders.

06:37.323 --> 06:40.243
So that's where we'll need
the eclipse advantage the most.

06:40.368 --> 06:42.662
When this is finished,
the Avatar

06:42.787 --> 06:44.872
would have defeated
the Fire Lord.

06:45.206 --> 06:47.917
We would have control
of the Fire Nation capital.

06:48.042 --> 06:50.920
And this war will be over!

06:51.045 --> 06:56.759
[ crowd cheering ]

06:56.884 --> 06:59.512
♪

07:11.816 --> 07:13.443
[ roars ]

07:13.568 --> 07:17.405
♪

07:24.996 --> 07:26.247
[ sheep baas ]

07:26.372 --> 07:32.170
♪

07:41.554 --> 07:45.725
♪

07:54.150 --> 07:55.568
We've been looking
everywhere for you.

07:55.693 --> 07:57.362
The boats are ready to leave.

07:57.487 --> 07:58.988
I messed up, Aang.

07:59.113 --> 08:00.323
What?

08:00.448 --> 08:02.617
The invasion plan
was my moment of truth.

08:02.742 --> 08:04.869
And I completely flopped it.

08:04.994 --> 08:07.705
I just...fell apart.

08:07.789 --> 08:10.458
Sokka, that speech wasn't
your moment of truth.

08:10.625 --> 08:11.959
That was just public speaking,

08:12.085 --> 08:13.836
and nobody's really good
at that.

08:13.920 --> 08:15.338
My dad is.

08:15.505 --> 08:18.299
He explained the plan perfectly
and inspired everyone.

08:18.424 --> 08:20.259
Like a real leader should.

08:20.385 --> 08:21.803
Look, your moment of truth

08:21.928 --> 08:24.055
isn't going to be
in front of some map.

08:24.180 --> 08:26.391
It's going to be out there
on the battlefield.

08:26.683 --> 08:28.643
You seem so confident
about everything.

08:28.768 --> 08:30.436
How do you know
we're going to win?

08:30.561 --> 08:33.314
Because I already failed
the world once at Ba Sing Se.

08:33.439 --> 08:35.316
I won't let myself fail again.

08:35.441 --> 08:39.112
♪

08:41.781 --> 08:42.824
BATO: There they are.

08:42.949 --> 08:44.867
The Great Gates of Azulon.

08:44.992 --> 08:47.120
KATARA: I don't
see any gates.

08:47.245 --> 08:48.788
Katara,
you and the Swamp-Benders

08:48.913 --> 08:50.456
whip up a fog cover.

08:50.581 --> 08:52.834
We'll sneak by that statues
just like we sneaked by

08:52.959 --> 08:54.669
that fire navy blockade.

08:54.794 --> 08:57.380
♪

09:05.471 --> 09:07.765
Keep it up,
we're almost through.

09:07.890 --> 09:12.353
[ alarm ringing ]

09:14.105 --> 09:16.357
[ fire blazing ]

09:16.858 --> 09:21.738
♪

09:34.083 --> 09:35.835
[ fire blazing ]

09:35.960 --> 09:38.755
♪

09:38.838 --> 09:40.381
[ motors revving ]

09:40.590 --> 09:41.924
Everyone below deck.

09:44.343 --> 09:46.262
Let's hope your invention works.

09:46.387 --> 09:51.476
♪

10:06.407 --> 10:08.367
[ crash ]

10:11.120 --> 10:12.663
No one's on board, Sir.

10:12.747 --> 10:13.790
Where'd they go?

10:13.998 --> 10:19.921
♪

10:26.052 --> 10:28.095
You really outdone
yourself this time, son.

10:28.221 --> 10:29.222
TOPH: Yeah.

10:29.347 --> 10:31.307
Congratulations, Sokka.

10:31.432 --> 10:34.852
You managed to invent a worse
way of travel than flying.

10:34.977 --> 10:36.187
Helmet?

10:36.312 --> 10:37.396
[ vomits ]

10:37.522 --> 10:38.815
Well, I just came up
with the idea.

10:38.898 --> 10:40.233
The Mechanist did all the work.

10:40.358 --> 10:42.443
But don't sell
yourself short, my boy.

10:42.568 --> 10:45.530
It was your idea
to use water-bending

10:45.655 --> 10:48.115
to make the subs sink and float.

10:48.241 --> 10:49.325
Brilliant!

10:49.450 --> 10:51.327
Though your original designs

10:51.452 --> 10:54.288
were a bit difficult
to decipher.

10:54.705 --> 10:57.750
Unfortunately, there is
one problem I couldn't fix.

10:58.125 --> 11:00.753
The subs have
a limited air supply.

11:00.878 --> 11:04.590
Before we land on the beaches,
we'll need to resurface.

11:06.926 --> 11:09.971
Lunchtime, General Iroh.

11:10.096 --> 11:12.807
And this time, I brought you
an extra bowl of rice.

11:12.932 --> 11:14.767
Thank you, Ming.

11:14.892 --> 11:17.603
Your little gestures of kindness

11:17.728 --> 11:21.315
have made my days in prison
bearable.

11:21.440 --> 11:24.944
I think you should take
the rest of the day off.

11:25.069 --> 11:28.114
- What?
- You don't look well.

11:28.239 --> 11:31.242
Maybe you should
go home and rest.

11:31.367 --> 11:33.202
No, I feel fine.

11:33.327 --> 11:34.579
Trust me.

11:34.704 --> 11:38.666
It is better that you are
not here this afternoon.

11:38.791 --> 11:44.422
♪

11:54.724 --> 11:56.851
So, this is it, huh?

11:57.226 --> 11:58.853
Are you ready
for the Fire Nation to know

11:58.936 --> 12:00.479
the Avatar's alive?

12:00.563 --> 12:01.689
I'm ready.

12:01.772 --> 12:06.027
♪

12:06.360 --> 12:09.572
I hope you kick some serious
Fire Lord butt, twinkle toes.

12:09.739 --> 12:11.240
HAKODA: Everyone, listen up.

12:11.699 --> 12:14.660
The next time we resurface,
it'll be on the beaches.

12:14.785 --> 12:16.829
So stay alert and fight smart.

12:17.121 --> 12:19.248
Now break time's over,
back in the subs.

12:19.415 --> 12:23.377
♪

12:26.130 --> 12:28.132
- Aang, I―
- Katara, I―

12:28.257 --> 12:29.675
You go first.

12:30.635 --> 12:33.054
We've been through
so many things together.

12:33.179 --> 12:35.806
And I've seen you
grow up so much.

12:36.098 --> 12:39.393
You're not that little goofy kid
I found in the iceberg anymore.

12:39.602 --> 12:41.312
I guess
what I'm trying to say is

12:41.437 --> 12:43.356
I'm really proud of you.

12:45.232 --> 12:47.401
Everything is going to be
different after today, isn't it?

12:47.526 --> 12:48.903
Yes, it is.

12:49.904 --> 12:52.990
What if―what if
I don't come back?

12:53.240 --> 12:54.742
Aang, don't say that.

12:54.867 --> 12:56.243
Of course you'll―

12:56.369 --> 13:01.666
♪

13:08.673 --> 13:09.674
Katara, what are you doing?

13:09.799 --> 13:11.217
It's time to submerge.

13:11.342 --> 13:13.594
What? Right, I'm on it.

13:13.719 --> 13:18.432
♪

13:18.557 --> 13:20.810
[ growls ]

13:20.935 --> 13:26.315
♪

13:29.777 --> 13:33.114
♪

13:33.239 --> 13:35.074
I'm sorry, Mai.

13:35.199 --> 13:41.122
♪

13:50.256 --> 13:51.340
[ munching ]

13:51.424 --> 13:52.466
What do you know?

13:52.550 --> 13:53.843
It did come in handy.

13:53.968 --> 13:59.932
♪

14:04.854 --> 14:05.980
Everyone in position.

14:06.105 --> 14:07.857
Earthbenders, into your tanks.

14:07.982 --> 14:09.608
This is going to be
a rough ride.

14:09.734 --> 14:14.947
♪

14:19.994 --> 14:23.039
[ alarm sounding ]

14:23.164 --> 14:27.501
♪

14:32.506 --> 14:36.594
[ crash and water rushing ]

14:36.802 --> 14:41.182
♪

14:48.272 --> 14:50.191
[ splash ]

14:50.775 --> 14:56.739
♪

14:57.323 --> 14:58.783
Ready the torpedo.

14:59.116 --> 15:02.536
♪

15:02.661 --> 15:04.288
Launch!

15:04.371 --> 15:07.249
♪

15:07.541 --> 15:11.629
[ explosion ]

15:12.296 --> 15:18.010
♪

15:28.771 --> 15:30.397
[ sighs ]

15:32.525 --> 15:37.321
[ missiles blasting ]

15:37.822 --> 15:44.120
♪

15:49.667 --> 15:50.751
MEN: [ screaming ]

15:55.464 --> 15:58.592
[ gunfire erupting ]

15:58.717 --> 16:04.223
♪

16:04.348 --> 16:08.936
[ gunfire continues ]

16:09.311 --> 16:14.567
♪

16:21.532 --> 16:22.992
[ roars ]

16:23.075 --> 16:28.664
♪

16:28.747 --> 16:29.874
[ fire blasts ]

16:29.999 --> 16:31.667
♪

16:31.792 --> 16:33.586
[ fire blasts ]

16:33.711 --> 16:40.509
♪

16:40.634 --> 16:43.262
[ metal crashing ]

16:43.387 --> 16:48.517
♪

16:57.526 --> 16:59.778
[ blast ]

16:59.904 --> 17:01.405
We're a man down.

17:01.530 --> 17:03.199
Where in tarnation is Hue?

17:05.242 --> 17:07.453
[ splash ]

17:07.578 --> 17:13.500
♪

17:21.717 --> 17:24.136
Hey Hue, where you been?

17:25.763 --> 17:27.890
Communing with nature.

17:28.015 --> 17:30.935
Takes a while to collect
this much seaweed.

17:31.060 --> 17:35.940
♪

17:46.075 --> 17:47.785
[ grunts ]

17:47.910 --> 17:49.370
Dad, look out!

17:49.495 --> 17:55.334
[ grunting ]

17:55.459 --> 18:00.756
♪

18:05.261 --> 18:07.179
[ explosion ]

18:07.304 --> 18:13.227
♪

18:13.352 --> 18:15.396
[ explosion ]

18:15.521 --> 18:17.523
Sokka, we've got
to take out those battlements.

18:17.648 --> 18:19.024
It's our only chance.

18:19.149 --> 18:20.484
I've got an idea.

18:20.609 --> 18:24.822
♪

18:24.947 --> 18:26.824
[ metal dings ]

18:26.949 --> 18:29.326
[ fuses sizzle ]

18:29.451 --> 18:30.828
♪

18:30.953 --> 18:32.037
MEN: Ah!

18:32.162 --> 18:37.626
♪

18:37.751 --> 18:39.378
Ah, ah!

18:39.503 --> 18:42.089
♪

18:42.214 --> 18:44.091
[ roaring ]

18:44.216 --> 18:45.467
You two take out
that battlement.

18:45.592 --> 18:46.635
I've got this one.

18:46.760 --> 18:48.137
Watch each other's backs.

18:48.262 --> 18:50.347
♪

18:50.472 --> 18:52.099
[ metal clings ]

18:52.224 --> 18:54.226
[ water rushing ]

18:54.351 --> 18:58.897
♪

18:59.023 --> 19:00.983
[ explosion ]

19:01.108 --> 19:05.279
♪

19:05.404 --> 19:08.407
[ grunting ]

19:08.532 --> 19:11.035
♪

19:11.160 --> 19:14.455
[ grunting ]

19:15.914 --> 19:17.082
Dad?

19:17.207 --> 19:18.250
Dad!

19:18.375 --> 19:22.504
♪

19:24.923 --> 19:27.760
I know I've made
some bad choices.

19:27.885 --> 19:29.428
But today...

19:29.553 --> 19:31.013
I'm gonna set things right.

19:31.138 --> 19:35.809
♪

19:41.982 --> 19:43.692
[ roars ]

19:43.817 --> 19:47.237
♪

19:47.363 --> 19:49.073
[ grunts ]

19:49.198 --> 19:52.993
[ water rushing ]

19:53.118 --> 19:54.495
KATARA: How does that feel, Dad?

19:54.620 --> 19:56.955
HAKODA: A-a little better.

19:57.081 --> 19:59.541
I need to get
back...to the troops.

19:59.666 --> 20:00.667
[ moaning ]

20:00.793 --> 20:02.544
KATARA: You're hurt...badly.

20:02.669 --> 20:04.088
You can't fight anymore.

20:04.588 --> 20:07.674
Everyone's counting on me
to lead this mission, Katara.

20:07.800 --> 20:10.094
I won't let them down.

20:10.219 --> 20:11.428
[ grunts ]

20:11.970 --> 20:13.847
Can't you heal him any faster?

20:13.972 --> 20:15.641
I'm doing everything I can.

20:15.766 --> 20:19.520
♪

20:19.645 --> 20:20.687
I'll do it.

20:21.063 --> 20:24.483
No offense, Sokka, but you're
not exactly Mr. Healing Hands.

20:24.775 --> 20:27.403
No, I'll lead
the invasion force.

20:27.611 --> 20:29.279
Don't be crazy, Sokka.

20:29.446 --> 20:32.449
Maybe I am a little crazy but
the eclipse is about to start,

20:32.574 --> 20:35.160
and we need to be up that
volcano by the time it does.

20:35.285 --> 20:37.037
HAKODA: You can do this.

20:37.621 --> 20:39.873
I'm proud of you, son.

20:41.166 --> 20:43.210
I still think you're crazy.

20:43.335 --> 20:44.837
But I'm proud of you, too.

20:44.962 --> 20:50.467
♪

20:50.592 --> 20:51.718
Yip yip.

20:51.844 --> 20:54.096
[ growls ]

20:54.221 --> 20:58.183
♪

20:58.308 --> 21:03.856
[ gunfire exploding ]

21:03.981 --> 21:06.942
♪

21:07.067 --> 21:08.652
Listen up, everyone!

21:08.777 --> 21:11.113
I want the tanks
in wedge formation!

21:11.238 --> 21:13.615
Warriors and benders
in the middle.

21:13.740 --> 21:16.452
We're taking that tower and
headed for the royal palace!

21:16.577 --> 21:21.957
♪

21:22.082 --> 21:24.501
[ gunfire exploding ]

21:24.626 --> 21:26.295
Charge!

21:26.420 --> 21:29.798
♪

21:31.675 --> 21:36.138
♪

21:43.729 --> 21:44.980
That's strange.

21:45.105 --> 21:49.776
♪

21:52.070 --> 21:53.280
[ door opens ]

21:53.405 --> 21:55.324
The Avatar is back!

22:00.329 --> 22:02.247
Hello?

22:02.372 --> 22:03.624
Anyone home?

22:04.082 --> 22:08.587
[ gunfire exploding ]

22:08.712 --> 22:13.342
♪

22:20.766 --> 22:24.269
[ explosion ]

22:24.394 --> 22:27.272
♪

22:27.397 --> 22:29.775
MEN: [ screaming ]

22:29.900 --> 22:34.154
[ gunfire exploding ]

22:34.279 --> 22:36.782
The Fire Nation
is falling back!

22:36.907 --> 22:38.867
♪

22:38.992 --> 22:41.870
Sokka, we're on
our way to victory.

22:41.995 --> 22:46.333
♪

22:57.636 --> 22:58.971
No.

22:59.096 --> 23:00.639
♪

23:00.764 --> 23:04.726
No, no, no!

23:04.851 --> 23:08.313
Fire Lord Ozai, where are you?

23:08.438 --> 23:09.898
♪

23:17.378 --> 23:21.883
MALE:
[ vocalizing drumbeats ]

23:27.805 --> 23:34.521
♪

23:50.870 --> 23:57.377
♪
